<!--
  Target display mode demo: display=target:<id> sends embeds to an
  external component (e.g. UseHistory sidebar) instead of rendering
  them inline in the chat.

  This is the recommended approach for sidebar activities.  For
  general-purpose field updates (not embeds), arrow syntax still works:
    sidebar -> some_content
-->
<Vertical>
  <SplitPanel sizes="65,35">
    <LeftPane>
      <Chat id="ChatTargetDemo" title="Target Demo" height="400px"><![CDATA[
title: Sidebar Embeds
cast:
  Kim:
    seed: kim_researcher
  Alex:
~~~~

Kim: Let's work through this step by step.

Kim: First, make a prediction about what you think will happen.

::prediction [display=target:sidebar label="Make your prediction"]

--- wait @prediction_input.value ---

Kim: Now let's see the actual results.

::results [display=target:sidebar label="View results"]

Alex: That's different from what I expected! [face=awe]
]]></Chat>
    </LeftPane>
    <RightPane>
      <UseHistory id="sidebar" initial="instructions" />
    </RightPane>
  </SplitPanel>

  <Hidden>
    <Markdown id="instructions">
Follow along with the conversation on the left.
Activities will appear here as you progress.
    </Markdown>
    <Vertical id="prediction">
      <Markdown>**Your Prediction**</Markdown>
      <TextArea id="prediction_input" placeholder="What do you think will happen?" />
    </Vertical>
    <Markdown id="results">
## Actual Results

The testing effect produced a **50% improvement** in retention
compared to re-reading.
    </Markdown>
  </Hidden>
</Vertical>
